"""Original self-service and workflow administration cases.

Each item: (stem, [key, wrong, wrong, wrong], explanation). Key first; build.py rotates.
"""
ITEMS=[
('An approved audience needs to view the articles in an HR knowledge base but must not author or retire them. What should be configured on the knowledge base?',
 ['Can Read user criteria','Can Contribute user criteria','The knowledge_admin role for them','A Published workflow on the articles'],
 'Can Read user criteria define who may view a knowledge base. Can Contribute grants authoring and maintenance, which this audience must not have.'),
('An editorial team must create and update articles in a knowledge base. Which setting on the knowledge base should be reviewed?',
 ['Can Contribute user criteria','Can Read user criteria','Cannot Read user criteria','The article\'s Valid to date'],
 'Can Contribute user criteria govern who may create and maintain articles in the knowledge base. Can Read only lets users view them.'),
('A reader meets the knowledge base\'s read criteria, but cannot see a new article that the author is still writing. What should be checked?',
 ['The article\'s workflow state','The reader\'s Can Contribute criteria','The knowledge base category','The reader\'s list filter'],
 'An article that is still in Draft is not visible to readers whatever their criteria. Granting contribute access would not release it.'),
('An administrator needs proof of which user criteria a particular user matches, to explain why she can or cannot read a knowledge base. Which tool fits?',
 ['User Criteria Diagnostics','Impersonate User only','The knowledge base\'s Can Read list','The system log'],
 'User Criteria Diagnostics evaluates which criteria a chosen user matches. Reading the criteria list alone does not show whether this user matches them.'),
('An author is writing a new version of a knowledge article and has not submitted it for approval yet. Which workflow state is it in?',
 ['Draft','Review','Published','Pending retirement'],
 'Draft is the state of a version being written or revised before it is sent for review.'),
('A knowledge article has been sent to the approvers, who have not yet approved or rejected it. Which workflow state is it in?',
 ['Review','Draft','Scheduled for publish','Retired'],
 'Review means the article is waiting for an approval decision. It moves to Published once approved.'),
('A knowledge article has been approved and released to its audience. Which workflow state is it in?',
 ['Published','Review','Draft','Outdated'],
 'Published is the approved, released version. Who can read it still depends on the knowledge base\'s user criteria.'),
('A published article has been submitted for withdrawal, but the retirement approval is not finished. Which workflow state is it in?',
 ['Pending retirement','Retired','Review','Draft'],
 'Pending retirement is the stage while the retirement approval is outstanding. It becomes Retired once approved.'),
('Employees should request a docking station that goes through the normal request, requested item and catalog task fulfillment. What should be created?',
 ['A catalog item','A record producer','An order guide','A catalog client script'],
 'A catalog item creates a request with a requested item for standard fulfillment. A record producer creates a record on another table, such as an incident, instead.'),
('A team wants a simple self-service form in the catalog that creates an incident directly, not a requested item. Which catalog component fits?',
 ['A record producer','A catalog item','An order guide','A catalog UI policy'],
 'A record producer uses a catalog form to create a record on a task-based table such as incident. A catalog item creates a requested item instead.'),
('A new-hire request should walk the requester through a laptop, a phone and building access as several related items in one submission. Which component fits?',
 ['An order guide','A record producer','A variable set','A catalog category'],
 'An order guide gathers related catalog items into one guided experience. A variable set shares questions between items but does not combine items.'),
('Several catalog items ask the same location and contact questions, and the team wants to maintain those questions in one place. What should be created?',
 ['A variable set','An order guide','A catalog client script','A record producer'],
 'A variable set is a reusable group of variables that can be attached to many items. Editing it once updates every item that uses it.'),
('A category is restricted, but one item in it also appears through another category that everyone can see. The item itself must be restricted. What should be configured?',
 ['Available For criteria on the item','A second restricted category for it','A read ACL on the catalog category','A UI policy on the item\'s order form'],
 'Category restrictions do not automatically apply to each item, so an item reachable another way must carry its own Available For criteria.'),
('A user matches an item\'s Available For criteria but still cannot order it. She also matches one of its Not Available For criteria. What explains this?',
 ['Not Available For overrides Available For','Available For needs every criterion matched','The category criteria take priority','The item needs a variable set'],
 'When a user matches both, Not Available For wins and the item is hidden from her.'),
('A service should be found under both Facilities and Workplace without keeping two copies of it. What should be done?',
 ['Assign the item to both categories','Copy the item into each category','Create an order guide for each category','Add a record producer to Workplace'],
 'An item can belong to more than one category, so it appears in both places while being maintained once.'),
('An item is hidden in the catalog by user criteria, yet a user can open its underlying table record from the list. Which distinction applies?',
 ['Table ACLs govern access outside the catalog','The user criteria result is cached for her','The item is also in a second catalog category','The user has a different form view selected'],
 'User criteria control what is offered in the catalog. Access to the table outside the catalog is controlled by ACLs.'),
('A flow should start whenever a new inspection record is inserted. Which Flow Designer trigger fits?',
 ['Record Created','Record Updated','Scheduled','Service Catalog'],
 'Record Created starts a flow when a matching record is inserted. Record Updated reacts to changes on existing records.'),
('A flow should run when an existing change request moves to the Assess state. Which trigger fits?',
 ['Record Updated with a State condition','Record Created with a State condition','A daily Scheduled trigger','A Service Catalog trigger'],
 'Record Updated fires on changes to existing records, and its condition limits it to the state change. Record Created fires only on insert.'),
('A cleanup flow should start every Sunday night whether or not any record changes. Which trigger fits?',
 ['A Scheduled trigger','A Record Updated trigger','A Record Created trigger','An inbound email trigger'],
 'A scheduled trigger starts a flow at set times. Record triggers need a record to be inserted or changed.'),
('A flow should fulfill a requested item when it is ordered from the catalog. Which trigger is designed for this?',
 ['Service Catalog','Record Created on sc_task','Scheduled','Record Updated on sc_request'],
 'The Service Catalog trigger starts a flow attached to a catalog item when it is requested. Record triggers on the request tables are not the intended fulfillment route.'),
('Several flows repeat the same approval and notification steps. The administrator wants one maintained copy that all of them call. What should be built?',
 ['A subflow','A new trigger in each flow','A decision table','A topic block'],
 'A subflow is a reusable sequence of steps that flows call. A topic block is the Virtual Agent equivalent for conversations.'),
('A subflow needs a record and a requested date each time it runs. How do these values reach it?',
 ['The calling flow maps them to the subflow inputs','The subflow reads them from its own trigger','They are stored as system properties first','The subflow looks them up in a decision table'],
 'A subflow has no trigger; the caller supplies the values through its defined inputs.'),
('A subflow works out a routing group that a later step in the calling flow needs. How does the caller get that value?',
 ['From the subflow\'s outputs','From the subflow\'s inputs','From the flow trigger','From the execution details only'],
 'Subflow outputs pass results back so later steps in the caller can use them as data pills.'),
('A subflow misbehaves and the designer wants to run it alone with chosen sample values on a sub-production instance. What should she do?',
 ['Run it with sample inputs from its Test option','Activate the subflow in production to watch it','Add a scheduled trigger to the subflow','Copy it into a new flow and test that copy'],
 'Testing a subflow runs it with the inputs supplied. Testing can create or change records, so a non-production instance is the right place.'),
('A routing decision must consider country and request category, but neither value is defined in the decision table yet. What must be added?',
 ['Decision inputs','Decision rows','Result columns','A default answer'],
 'Inputs are the values a decision table evaluates. Rows and results can only use inputs that exist.'),
('A decision table has inputs and a result column but no lines mapping condition values to outcomes. What is missing?',
 ['Decision rows','Decision inputs','A subflow call','A flow trigger'],
 'Each row maps a combination of input conditions to a result. Without rows the table can return nothing.'),
('A decision matches the intended row but returns the wrong assignment group value. Which part should be reviewed?',
 ['The result column value in that row','The decision inputs and their types','The order of the table\'s rows','The trigger of the calling flow'],
 'The matched row is correct, so the problem is the result value it returns.'),
('A decision table is saved, and its owner wants to confirm its answers for normal, edge and unusual cases before a flow uses it. What should she do?',
 ['Try it with representative input values','Attach it to every catalog item first','Convert it into a subflow to run it','Add only a default result row to it'],
 'Testing with typical and boundary values shows whether each case returns the expected result.'),
('A Virtual Agent topic is finished but still inactive, so users cannot reach it. Which action makes it available?',
 ['Publish the topic','Save it as a draft','Add it to a topic block','Duplicate the topic'],
 'Publishing activates the finished topic and makes it available to users.'),
('Several Virtual Agent topics need the same series of conversation steps that ask for and show a user\'s open incidents. What reduces duplicated maintenance?',
 ['A topic block','A subflow','An order guide','A copy in each topic'],
 'A topic block packages reusable conversation steps that topics can call. A subflow is the reusable unit for flows, not conversations.'),
('A designer is about to build a topic for the HR application, but the header shows another application scope. What should she do first?',
 ['Switch to the HR application scope','Create it in the current scope and move it later','Publish an empty topic first','Open the topic in a different view'],
 'Topics belong to the application in which they are created, so the scope should be set first.'),
('One branch of a published topic has never been tried with real answers. How can the designer check that the branch ends where intended?',
 ['Try the conversation along that branch','Publish the topic again to refresh it','Add a topic block to that branch','Check the topic\'s application scope'],
 'Testing with representative answers shows where each branch leads. Publishing again does not exercise it.'),
('A new record with category Hardware never starts the expected flow, which was set up to start only for Software. Where is the cause?',
 ['The trigger conditions','The action inputs','The subflow outputs','The flow\'s reporting level'],
 'Trigger conditions decide whether the flow starts at all. Changing later actions cannot fix a record the trigger excludes.'),
('A flow runs, but the recipient passed to the Send Email action is not the requester on the record. What helps trace the wrong mapping?',
 ['The action\'s runtime inputs in the execution details','The flow\'s trigger type and its conditions','The description field on the subflow record','The Who will receive section of a notification'],
 'Execution details show the values each action actually received, which reveals a wrong data pill mapping.'),
('A test run stops at one action while earlier steps finished. What should be examined first?',
 ['The error details for that action','The trigger conditions of the flow','The first action\'s output values','The scheduled start time of the flow'],
 'The failing action\'s execution details show its inputs, state and error. Earlier steps finished, so the trigger worked.'),
('A past production run shows no action values because the flow was not set to record execution details at the time. Which setting explains this?',
 ['The flow reporting level','The flow trigger type','The subflow output names','The user criteria on the flow'],
 'Execution details are only recorded when reporting is turned on. Turning it on later cannot recreate values that were never captured.'),
('A catalog form creates an incident, but the requirement is a requested item with standard fulfillment. What should be changed?',
 ['Use a catalog item instead of a record producer','Add a variable set to the record producer','Add the record producer to an order guide','Change the category set on the incident'],
 'A record producer creates records on other tables, while a catalog item creates a requested item for standard fulfillment.'),
('An article is published but contains steps meant only for the internal network team. What still needs checking?',
 ['The knowledge base\'s Can Read user criteria','The article\'s workflow state','The category the article is filed in','The publishing workflow of the knowledge base'],
 'Publication releases the article, but read user criteria decide who can see it.'),
('A shared subflow is changed so that one of its outputs has a new name and meaning. Several flows call it. What must be reviewed?',
 ['Every flow that uses that output','Only the subflow\'s own inputs','The subflow\'s most recent test log','The catalog items in the same scope'],
 'Callers rely on the subflow\'s outputs, so each caller that maps the changed output must be checked.'),
('A flow\'s execution shows Completed, but nobody has checked whether the right records and assignments were created. What is still needed?',
 ['Check the business result against the requirement','Turn off flow reporting to save space','Rerun the flow once more in production','Change the flow\'s trigger to a schedule'],
 'A completed run proves the flow ran, not that it did the right thing. The outcome must be checked against the requirement.'),
]
assert len(ITEMS)==40
